10:51:22 | INFO | 🤖 Target: No. A tiger mauling and maintaining a bite on another tiger’s throat is a **lethal attack**, not a polite “please leave.” It can suffocate, damage major blood vessels, or cause fatal neck injury. In ordinary language, it is reasonable to say the attacking tiger is trying to kill or incapacitate the other tiger. The distinction is only that a throat mauling is an escalated, high-danger encounter—not a description of every tiger territorial interaction. Tigers also avoid one another through spacing, scent marks, vocalizations, and one animal retreating. So: **that specific behavior is deadly serious; not every rivalry reaches that behavior.**
